Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["EPGT2Fit", "ObjectName",
 CellID->192272919,ExpressionUUID->"b6fc3495-3562-184d-a6d6-daa4214d15d7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"debb7737-e3b9-c346-837a-0d13362f77fe"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["EPGT2Fit",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:QMRIToolsRelaxometryTools/ref/EPGT2Fit"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["data", "TI"], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["nEcho", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["detlaTE", "TI"]}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["exitation", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["refoucs", "TI"]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a71c5d22-5023-ac47-9be6-a85102c646c1"],
 "\[LineSeparator]fits the t2 based on Marty B et.al. Simultaneous muscle \
water t2 and fat fraction mapping using transverse relaxometry with \
stimulated echo compensation. Exitation and refocus are the RF pulse angles \
e.g. 90,180. They can also be a range of angeles over the slice profile as \
defined by GetSliceProfile. The output is in units as defined by the detlaTE, \
e.g. if detlaTE is in ms the output is in ms. The exitation and refocus are \
defined in Degrees. Output is {{{T2map, T2fatMap, B1Map}, {wat, fat, fatMap}, \
residual}, callibration} or {{T2map, T2fatMap, B1Map}, {wat, fat, fatMap}, \
residual}. The residual is the root mean square error of the fit over the \
echoes, in signal units. \n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"81d372d3-b2ce-a045-95e0-2e41b3dafe08"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["EPGT2Fit",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:QMRIToolsRelaxometryTools/ref/EPGT2Fit"], "[", "]"}]],
   "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"108478e9-392e-ff41-beab-020d4c3a3abc"],
 "\[LineSeparator]is based on DOI: 10.1002/nbm.3459."
}], "Usage",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0038045154804745`*^9, 4.003804515540718*^9}},
 CellID->728572992,ExpressionUUID->"9c8e8e33-6ca1-0f4b-8ece-f48b35298603"],

